## Bug fixed: unescaped filename in `Content-Disposition` (gin/context.go, `FileAttachment`)

### Root cause
`Context.FileAttachment` interpolated the caller-supplied filename directly into a quoted-string header value:

```go
c.Writer.Header().Set("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename="`+filename+`"`)
```

Any `"` or `\` in the filename breaks the header (and allows header/parameter injection). Repro (temp test I authored, since deleted) with `c.FileAttachment("./gin.go", `new"filename.go`)`:
- before: `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="new"filename.go"`  ← broken, `mime.ParseMediaType` fails / wrong filename
- after:  `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="new\"filename.go"` ← parses back to `new"filename.go`
- backslash: before `back\slash.txt` (unescaped), after `back\\slash.txt` (parses back correctly)

### Change (only region touched: /gin/context.go lines 1037–1056)
```diff
@@ -1034,11 +1034,19 @@ func (c *Context) FileFromFS(filepath string, fs http.FileSystem) {
 	http.FileServer(fs).ServeHTTP(c.Writer, c.Request)
 }

